    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d168">

                <pb facs="0380" n="122" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg122"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.0151/50</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-02-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 04, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1182. From The Hague: “The Netherlands Government has positive information from
                    London that the British Admiralty now furnishes arms to merchant vessels for
                    resistance on ground that the German regulations sanction the same measure for
                    German merchant vessels.” Please confirm this.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
